{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"75d70721","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.007418,"end_time":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.297653+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.290235+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Breast Cancer Diagnosis Classification on the Wisconsin Diagnostic Dataset (WDBC)\n","\n","**Objective.** Classify breast tumours as benign or malignant from 30 numeric features computed from digitised images of fine needle aspirates (569 patients: 357 benign and 212 malignant). Ten cell nucleus measurements (radius, texture, perimeter, area, smoothness, compactness, concavity, concave points, symmetry and fractal dimension) are each reported as a mean (`_mean`), a standard error (`_se`) and a worst value (`_worst`) across the cells in an image.\n","\n","**Background.** The notebook extends a published comparison of eight classifiers on a small clinical dataset (La Moglia and Almustafa, 2025), whose future work section called for larger data. The full pipeline is run on WDBC, a dataset almost three times larger than the clinical one, with no missing values, no placeholder characters and no categorical columns. The same eight classifiers are used, so results stay comparable with the reference study.\n","\n","**Improvements over the reference study**\n","\n","| Limitation of the reference study | Addressed by | Step |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| No cross validation | Stratified 5 fold cross validation | 7 |\n","| No hyperparameter tuning | Grid search inside nested cross validation | 8 and 9 |\n","| No significance testing | Paired t tests with Holm correction, and McNemar's test | 10 |\n","| Small sample size | Whole pipeline run on a larger dataset | 2 to 14 |\n","| Manual feature selection | Cross validated, SHAP based feature selection | 12 |\n","| Unstable LightGBM results | Stability check across feature counts | 13 |\n","\n","**Models and metrics.** Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Extra Trees, XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost, SVC and Gaussian Naive Bayes. Balanced accuracy is the main metric, with recall, precision, F1 and ROC AUC reported alongside it.\n","\n","**Requirements.** Attach the Kaggle dataset `uciml/breast-cancer-wisconsin-data` and check that `DATA_PATH` in Step 2 matches the mounted path. The notebook runs on CPU and needs internet access to install packages.\n","\n","**Contents**\n","\n","1. Setup\n","2. Data loading and cleaning\n","3. Exploratory data analysis\n","4. Feature matrix and train/test split\n","5. Classifier definitions\n","6. Baseline evaluation on the held out test split\n","7. Stratified cross validation\n","8. Hyperparameter tuning with nested cross validation\n","9. Final tuned models\n","10. Statistical significance testing\n","11. Cross dataset ranking check\n","12. SHAP based feature selection\n","13. LightGBM stability across feature counts\n","14. Consolidated results\n","15. Extension: stacking ensemble and MLP baseline\n","16. Summary"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8f3012e8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006676,"end_time":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.310789+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.304113+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Step 1: Setup"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"72cd0805","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.326381Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.326038Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-22T11:31:03.088098Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-22T11:31:03.086456Z"},"papermill":{"duration":5.77193,"end_time":"2026-10-22T11:31:03.090279+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T11:30:57.318349+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# Packages that are not preinstalled in the Kaggle image\n","!pip install -q shap lightgbm catboost xgboost statsmodels"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"e2248a05","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-22T11:31:03.1077Z","iopub.status.bu